# beatmania IIDX with DDR 2nd Club Version (896 VER. JAB), Konami 1999: the club kit's IIDX cabinet
# (1st style board, Twinkle). First power-on from blank NVRAM, as bmiidxc-boot.his, but the backup
# is cleared in test mode (the 1P Start clear of the device check resets the machine through the
# watchdog and leaves E150, in MAME too). Test mode: BACKUP CLEAR (the eighth item), yes; NETWORK
# OPTIONS (the DDR club link: GAME JOINING PERIOD 10, MAX STAGE (CLUB PLAY) 3) and its NETWORK
# CHECK with no DDR cabinet on the cable (PROTOCOL VERSION 1.0, CABLE STATUS --------, RECEIVE
# STATUS DNC); exits, TEST EXIT, yes; the game resets itself (the watchdog) and boots to attract.
# SW1/SW2 move the cursor down/up, SW6 does, SW7 exits; SW2 answers yes. Hashes the main RAM every
# frame and snapshots every 60 frames, against MAME with the DVD player's CTS on SIO1 (the
# oracle's patch, PLAN.md section 21, TW-5).
game bmiidxc

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 2400 press "Test" 8
from 0 every 60 snap
# BACKUP CLEAR: seven down, do, yes
at 2900 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 2930 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 2960 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 2990 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3020 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3050 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3080 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3150 press "P1-6 (SW6)" 8
at 3210 press "P1-2 (SW2)" 8
# NETWORK OPTIONS: one down, do; NETWORK CHECK: two down, do; exit both
at 3810 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3870 press "P1-6 (SW6)" 8
at 3950 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3980 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 4010 press "P1-6 (SW6)" 8
at 4400 press "P1-7 (SW7)" 8
at 4500 press "P1-7 (SW7)" 8
# TEST EXIT, yes: the reset, then the boot to attract
at 4700 press "P1-7 (SW7)" 8
at 4760 press "P1-2 (SW2)" 8
at 10800 quit
